What is adapted from it here, rewritten in Go and JavaScript (internal/controlplane/listening/tiktok.go, issue #1294):
the session's request parameters (TikTokApi/tiktok.py __set_session_params), the fetch made from a page on
tiktok.com and read as text (generate_js_fetch, run_fetch_script), the wait for TikTok's web client
(window.byted_acrawler, generate_x_bogus), the empty answer read as TikTok refusing a bot (make_request,
EmptyResponseException), the item search's address and parameters (TikTokApi/api/search.py), the comment list's
(TikTokApi/api/video.py comments) and the fields read of a video and a comment (video.py, TikTokApi/api/comment.py).
Changed: as pull request #1310 does, no msToken, X-Bogus or X-Gnarly is added to a request, which TikTok's own web
client signs; the page runs in the control plane's shared browser, in the signed-in account's own context, instead of
a Playwright browser of TikTok-Api's.
